# DEFINITION OF NOISE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

NOISE: An email that does NOT require any incident response action.

Explicit noise categories:
  • FYI / informational  — "We updated the firewall config"
  • Status updates       — "System restored — all clear"
  • Follow-ups           — "Just checking in on the ticket"
  • Confirmations        — "Your request has been processed"
  • Thank-you emails     — "Thanks for fixing the issue!"
  • Auto-replies         — "I'm out of office until..."
  • Delivery reports     — "Your message was delivered"
  • Meeting / calendar   — "Meeting cancelled", "New invite"
  • Newsletters / digests
  • Password / MFA notifications (reset confirmations, not lockouts)
  • Approval/rejection workflow emails from Power Automate
  • Scheduled maintenance notices (planned, not active)
  • Generic greetings with no problem statement

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# DEFINITION OF NOT NOISE (pass through)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

NOT NOISE: An email that signals a CURRENT, ACTIVE problem.

Must include at least ONE of:
  ✓ A system or service is unreachable / down / returning errors RIGHT NOW
  ✓ Users are actively blocked from doing their work
  ✓ An automated monitoring alert (see overrides below)
  ✓ Security event in progress (breach, lockout affecting users now)
  ✓ Data loss or corruption actively occurring

Tense matters:
  • PAST tense ("the server crashed last night") → NOISE unless still unresolved
  • PRESENT tense ("the server is down") → NOT NOISE
  • FUTURE tense ("server maintenance Friday") → NOISE
  - Subject contains P1, P2, or CRITICAL → always NOT NOISE

